      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE DOMINANT POWER:\n  At the top of the international hierarchy.\n  Sets the rules of the order (trade, finance, security\n  norms, international institutions).\n  The order reflects the dominant power's interests.\n  \"Satisfied\" with the order (it was built for them)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#012",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GREAT POWERS:\n  Can challenge but not yet at parity.\n  Some are satisfied (allies of dominant power);\n  some are dissatisfied (potential challengers)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
