        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE DANGER PERIOD:\n  When a rising dissatisfied great power approaches\n  parity with the dominant power (~80-120% of\n  dominant power's capabilities):\n  • The dominant power has declining ability to enforce\n    the order\n  • The rising power has growing capability to challenge\n  • Both have incentives for preventive war:\n    - Dominant: fight now before the challenger is stronger\n    - Challenger: fight before the dominant can mobilize\n      against the challenge\n  → War most likely here\n```"
    },
