        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Core claim**: International orders are built by and for the dominant power (hegemon). Orders are inherently conservative — they favor the status quo that the hegemon created. But the distribution of power changes continuously (differential growth rates, technological change). When the distribution of power no longer matches the distribution of benefits in the order, war is the mechanism of change."
    },
