        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nGILPIN'S CHANGE MECHANISM\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#020",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PHASE 1: HEGEMONIC ORDER\n  Dominant power creates order (institutions, norms,\n  rules) that serves its interests.\n  Challenger states grow under this order\n  (free riding on public goods; economic development)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#021",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PHASE 2: POWER SHIFT\n  Differential growth rates: the challenger grows\n  faster than the hegemon (often because it is\n  growing from a lower base; also because it\n  can free-ride on hegemonic public goods).\n  Technology shifts advantage.\n  The hegemon faces: aging infrastructure, costly\n  global commitments, declining growth rate."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#022",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "section": "international-relations",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Power Transition Theory and Hegemonic Wars",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PHASE 3: DISSATISFACTION\n  The rising challenger finds the existing order\n  does not serve its interests.\n  The rules were written for the old hegemon.\n  The challenger wants a different order."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md#023",
      "path": [
        "05-POWER-TRANSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:international-relations:05-power-transition, git-history:international-relations:05-power-transition]",
        "canonical_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[power, transition]",
        "current_path": "international-relations/05-POWER-TRANSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:international-relations:power-transition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "international-relations",
